# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit a real key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit .env, then:
#   python3 check_api.py          # verifies the key without starting anything
#   python3 run_web.py            # reads .env at startup
#
# The ONLY secret this project uses. It drafts interview questions from a
# candidate's CV and nothing else: the cameras, the transcript, the
# measurement, the ratings and the consent flow all work without it. Leaving
# it unset is a supported configuration -- the question card says so and the
# interview runs. config.generation.enabled = False removes the feature and
# its data egress entirely.
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
#
# Get one from https://aistudio.google.com, or in the Google Cloud console:
# APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API KEY, on a
# project with the Generative Language API enabled.
#
# It must be an API KEY. That page also lists OAuth 2.0 Client IDs and
# Service Accounts, and neither can authenticate a request here:
#   - a client id ends ".apps.googleusercontent.com" and identifies an app
#   - a service account is a JSON file or a PEM block
#   - "ya29..." is a short-lived access token
# All four are rejected before any request, by name, so a wrong paste is
# diagnosed rather than reported as an invalid key.
#
# Formats vary and change: keys starting "AIza" (39 chars) and "AQ." (53) are
# both valid. Nothing here whitelists a prefix -- an earlier version required
# "AIza" and rejected a working key.
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is accepted as an alternative name; that is what gcloud
# exports. If both are set, GEMINI_API_KEY wins.
#
# An exported shell variable outranks this file by design, so a stale export
# silently shadows a correct .env. That case is detected and named.

# Which model drafts the questions: config.generation.gemini_model, which
# defaults to the alias "gemini-pro-latest" so it does not go stale. A pinned
# id can be retired -- gemini-2.5-pro was, and still appeared in the model
# listing afterwards.
#
#   python3 check_api.py --list-models
#
# lists what the key can see, though the listing includes retired models, so
# only a real request proves callability. The audit trail records which model
# actually answered, not the alias.

# Optional. Raises the GitHub profile panel's rate limit from 60 requests an
# hour for the whole machine to 5000. See github_profile.py.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
